# Deployment (`apps/marketing`, `apps/docs`, `vercel.json`)

- Both apps are [Vercel Services](https://vercel.com/docs/services) of one project, declared in the root `vercel.json`.
- The marketing app (`apps/marketing`) owns `/`, `/_next`, `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `manifest.webmanifest` and `/.well-known/security.txt` (RFC 9116, `Expires` 180 days ahead, cached for a day).
- Marketing owns `/create`, the preset builder: a static shell whose client component reads `?preset=` and runs `permdock/preset` in the browser. Marketing also owns `/r`, the `@permdock` shadcn registry: `shadcn build` writes `public/r/*.json` from `apps/marketing/registry.json` before `next build` (gitignored, never committed), and `app/r/[name]/route.ts` answers `/r/preset-<code>.json` from `permdock/preset`. Static files are served before the dynamic route. Marketing owns `/schemas/*`, the `$id` of every `permdock` wire schema: `scripts/schemas.ts` copies the package's `schemas/*.json` into `public/schemas/` before `next build` and `next dev` (gitignored), and `next.config.ts` adds `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` there. `vercel.json` needs no entry because `/schemas/*` falls to the marketing catch-all. Recipe sources live in `apps/marketing/registry/` and type-check against `packages/ui` with `registry/tsconfig.json` (web) and `registry/tsconfig.native.json` (React Native Reusables stubs).
- The docs app keeps `/docs` (including `/docs/sitemap.xml`, `/docs/ask`, `/docs/changelog`, the `/docs/api/chat` Ask AI endpoint, the `/docs/mcp` docs MCP server, and `/docs/llms.txt` and `/docs/llms-full.txt`, rewritten to the root files), `/api/search`, `/devtools`, `/llms.txt`, `/llms-full.txt`, `/llms.mdx`, `/og`, `/docs.md` and the BotID challenge path (`/149e9513-…`, rewritten by `withBotId`), with `assetPrefix: '/docs'` so its assets ride `/docs/_next`. Never `basePath: '/docs'`, which double-prefixes `next/link`. Marketing redirects `/changelog` and `/blog/*` to `/docs/changelog`.
- Both apps spread `createNextConfig()` from `packages/next-config` (security headers, `allowedDevOrigins`, Sentry options) and import UI from `packages/ui` through `transpilePackages`. Links between the two apps are plain anchors (`SiteLink`), never `next/link`.
- `/docs/api/chat` calls the AI Gateway over Vercel OIDC. Never set `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` or a provider key. On Vercel it first checks BotID and the `docs-ask-ai` rate-limit rule (`@vercel/firewall`); the rule lives in the Vercel Firewall, and while it is missing Ask AI answers 503.
- Markdown negotiation is `rewrites().beforeFiles` in `apps/docs/next.config.ts`: `.md` suffixes, and an `Accept` header that lists markdown before `text/html`. There is no `proxy.ts`.
- Both services build with `turbo run build --filter=<service>`, which compiles `permdock` first because `dist/` is not committed. Vercel's bundled pnpm fails the `devEngines` pnpm check, so the install command activates the `devEngines` pnpm version itself and installs only the service, its workspace dependencies and the root tooling (`--frozen-lockfile --filter '{.}...' --include-workspace-root`), and the build command puts a corepack `pnpm` shim first on `PATH` because turbo spawns `pnpm` for each task.
- Each service's `ignoreCommand` runs `turbo query affected --packages <service> --exit-code` against `VERCEL_GIT_PREVIOUS_SHA` and skips the build only when nothing is affected. A turbo error or a missing base ref builds. `vercel.json` is a build input of both services, so a change to it rebuilds both.
- `git.deploymentEnabled` deploys `main` only: `*` and `**` are off (`*` does not cross `/`), and so is `changeset-release/*`. Add `develop` when it exists. Keys are minimatch globs.
- Functions run in `fra1` (`regions`).
- `/docs/mcp` is the public docs MCP server: search and page-fetch only, no subject.
- PermDock Cloud is a separate Vercel project in the `PermDock-Cloud` repository: dashboard `https://app.permdock.com`, API `https://permdock.com/api`, read-only MCP `https://permdock.com/mcp`. `vercel.json` rewrites `/api/(.*)`, `/mcp`, `/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/api` and `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp` to `https://app.permdock.com`, before the `/(.*)` marketing catch-all; `/api/search` stays on docs and comes first. `pnpm docs:drift` checks the order. These routes need no `next dev` rewrite: Cloud is a separate project, so `apps/marketing/next.config.ts` rewrites only the docs service.
- Local: `pnpm dev:portless` serves marketing at `https://permdock.localhost`, which proxies `/docs` to `https://docs.permdock.localhost` (`.agents/rules/local-dev-portless-agent-browser.mdc`). Without Portless, `pnpm dev:marketing` serves marketing on `:3000` and docs on `:3001`; `pnpm dev:docs` runs the docs alone.
